  "description": "Software installed and run as a non-privileged user may conduct improper GPU system calls causing a stack overflow in the kernel. The overflow occurs when processing resolved Linux/Android fence synchronization checkpoints, while user checkpoints are excluded from the stack array. Successful exploitation can cause kernel memory corruption and typically results in a denial-of-service condition through a kernel crash.\n\n\n\nThe code vulnerability is a buffer write beyond the allocated array on the stack caused by copying excessive data from an internal buffer.",
